WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.120
A while ago I made a video

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:01.800
The topic was

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.640
Why you should start

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:04.640
Vibe Coding immediately

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.480
At the end, I introduced my new startup project

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.960
An AI community

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.320
As a result, this video became my most controversial one since I started YouTube.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.600
one of the most controversial.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.640
I received a lot of negative comments

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.560
So much so that some fans sent me private messages to express their support.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.840
caring about my mental state

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.680
I hope I won't be hurt by these comments.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.640
When I saw these private messages

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.640
My first reaction was of course very touched.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.600
Thank you for your concern.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.280
My second reaction was

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.160
I found it very interesting.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.160
Just as I replied to them

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.040
Actually, don't worry.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.760
I was not affected.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.320
Because what you see

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.120
It's just some noise.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.760
And the signals I see and the comment section

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.080
The feeling it gives people is just the opposite.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.600
The contrast between them

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.960
made me realize an interesting and important question

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.560
That is, if we can't

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.920
If we separate noise from signal,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.720
It's very likely to be misled by noise

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.520
Make wrong judgments and decisions

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.480
and even go down the wrong path.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.920
Especially in today's information explosion era

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:04.120
Having your own signal filter is crucial.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.120
So I think I should make a video

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.720
to combine this startup with some of my life experiences

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:09.720
Share with everyone

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:14.400
5 mental models that help me distinguish between signals and noise in life

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.720
I hope it can bring some inspiration to everyone.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.120
The first mental model that helps me distinguish between noise and signal is

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:23.920
Always remember the 1% rule in a crowd.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.640
This so-called 1% rule

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:28.240
It says that in a community on the Internet

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.840
or among the entire audience

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.720
90% of people are lurkers

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.000
The silent majority

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.280
They just browse passively

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.760
Only 10% of people may interact

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.080
And among them, only 1% of people

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.280
contributed most of the interactive content.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.920
This means that very few people

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.920
often have a disproportionate impact.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.480
So you have to realize

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.520
What you see on the surface is not equal to the truth.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.880
So those comments in my YouTube comment section

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.040
often come from this 1% of people.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.280
And more importantly,

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:01.720
On the internet, negative emotions spread more strongly.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.400
It's like when you go to a restaurant's Google review to see

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.840
If someone thinks it's good

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.480
He probably won't leave a comment.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.920
But if the experience is not good

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:12.960
Anger will motivate people to be more willing to make negative comments.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.280
In fact, our entire internet is now full of negative emotions.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.040
These emotions are very easily passed through this 1% of people.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.680
showcased in a concentrated way.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.480
This will make you feel that the world is very bad.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.000
Bad news everywhere

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.320
Every time I go back to my country, I get asked

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.080
Is Canada still safe?

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.560
If you can't make it, just come back home.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.640
At this point you will find

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.480
Originally living in Canada

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.560
and the Canada that others see in the news

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.280
are two different worlds.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.440
Actually, the truth is

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:41.200
This 1% of voices are disproportionately amplified.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.040
People think what they see is a signal

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:45.200
But what you actually get may be noise.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.880
But just knowing that what you see is not necessarily the truth

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.120
is far from enough.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.840
He can only tell you that this may be noise.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:56.080
But what are the real signals?

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.280
First of all, I think you should try to get

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.440
The data of the 90% silent majority.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.960
Let's talk about my video.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.800
Although the comment section may be full of scolding

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.280
But the backend data shows

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:09.160
The approval rate is nearly 94%.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.640
And this video also gained me nearly 3,000 followers.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.240
So these data representing the silent majority

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.120
formed a huge contrast with the emotions in the comment section.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:18.960
This is why

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.120
My physical feeling is very different from the audience who cares about me.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.560
But for me,

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.120
These data are still not the most accurate signals.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.520
I want to find more core and direct information.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.960
We need to introduce my second mental model.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.520
That is, transactions are often the most real signals.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.520
The so-called transaction is to vote with money.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.440
Because verbal support and opposition are very easy.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:44.400
But only when people are willing to pay the actual cost

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.160
The signal they convey is the most real.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:51.000
Then I would like to share a little story about the new community this time.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.560
I was actually very nervous after the video was released.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.400
I'm eager to know the clearest signal.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:01.320
That is, how many people will pay to join this community.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.600
As you all know, I have my own book club community.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:05.680
A mouthful of new rice

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.600
It went online more than two years ago.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.880
That was very interesting at the time.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.240
The announcement video was less than 6 minutes long.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:14.520
Someone had already joined 30 seconds after it went live.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.040
The video is not over yet.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:19.320
Dozens of people have already paid to become founding members.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.760
But this time it's a little different.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.720
This video is over 20 minutes long.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.080
I didn't mention this new community until the very end.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.280
Of course I was thinking

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.080
When will the first person to pay appear?

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.760
As soon as the video was released, I started playing it simultaneously.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.360
staring at the screen nervously

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.640
No one came in for 5 minutes.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.160
No one came in for 10 minutes.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:37.960
Still no one came in after 15 minutes.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.440
I was a little self-doubting at the time.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.800
Did I screw this up?

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:44.720
Interestingly, at the exact moment the video ended

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:45.920
The first person came in.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:48.240
Then my phone kept sending reminders.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.720
The second, the third, the tenth, the hundredth.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.200
Online for 72 hours

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.800
We have over 700 paying members.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.960
Nearly 1,400 after three weeks.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.960
This is for me and my co-creation partners.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.280
is the most accurate signal.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:03.000
We know that at least we didn't screw this up.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:06.520
So why do I value transaction data so much?

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.920
and ignore those negative comments?

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.760
This is what my years of entrepreneurial and life experience have taught me.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:14.000
That is, when possible,

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.640
I should try to get signals through transactions as much as possible.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:21.040
This is because in a normally functioning society

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:24.640
Money is a very direct and accurate signal.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.200
If you put in a lot of effort

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:27.600
You think you're going in the right direction.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:31.040
But no one pays for the product or service you launch.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.800
Then this could be an important signal.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.640
You might be doing something wrong somewhere.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.960
A while ago I was chatting with members of the community.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.520
We talked about making YouTube videos.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:42.240
I said the biggest mistake I made on YouTube was

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.440
is not being able to commercialize it sooner.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.720
When I first started on YouTube

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.680
I'm purely passionate, just sharing.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.080
But there's a problem here.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.800
My passion, my self-perceived value

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.040
These things can't give me an accurate signal.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.680
It wasn't until later that I realized a sentence.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:03.120
That is, only things that make money have vitality.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:05.240
I'm not encouraging profit-seeking here.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:06.000
What I want to say is

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:09.520
Even if you are doing the most selfless and sincere sharing

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.960
If it doesn't make money

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.800
Then this matter may not be sustainable.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.600
If I don't consider monetization

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.640
I can't even cover the filming costs.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:18.880
I'm losing money.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:21.280
This will make things very difficult.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.160
More importantly,

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.480
If there is no transaction

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.040
You can't even get an accurate signal.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.920
This will leave you in deep confusion.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.400
Can't find the right direction.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.120
And the mistake I made for a long time was

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.640
I didn't even give others a chance.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:37.520
Let others help me monetize.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:41.480
I call this disease "performing without getting paid".

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:42.320
So what does that mean?

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:44.960
You've all seen street performers, right?

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.040
When they are performing

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.600
They often put their hats or rice bowls on the ground.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.640
Let everyone give some money.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.040
It has a behavior that promotes transactions.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:53.960
But what I observed is

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:56.600
Many of our YouTubers don't do this.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.880
We put a lot of effort into showing off our skills.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:01.160
But never put the hat on the ground.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.360
What we do is more like

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.240
You're performing on the street.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.560
I hope the fruit stand owner next to me sells his fruit and then

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:06.680
give you some money.

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:10.160
But the fruit stand owner makes money by selling his own products.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.360
That's a signal to him.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.400
Not a signal to you.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:14.840
For a long time

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:18.640
I'm the one who performs without putting his hat on the ground.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:23.120
So the advice I want to give to everyone who wants to be a YouTuber is

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.920
Before you make your first video

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.480
You have to think clearly

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:27.840
Where is my rice bowl?

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.800
Do I have a hat that I can put on the ground?

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.440
In the process of monetizing my YouTube channel

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:34.320
Besides having your own products

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.240
My hat

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:38.440
Getting sponsorship is also a very important part.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.240
And in my interactions with them

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:41.840
also deeply confirms

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.120
A transaction is a signal.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.640
The pressure of making a sponsored video is actually quite high.

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:48.360
Because you want to prove your worth.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.440
So we often focus on the number of views.

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:52.920
I had a very interesting experience once.

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:54.560
A sponsor sponsored one of my videos.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:56.840
As a result, the number of views was very poor.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.480
I was a little disappointed in myself at the time.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:00.120
Even a little ashamed.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:03.160
I thought they would definitely not come to me again in the future.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.680
But I didn't expect that a week after the video was released

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:07.880
This sponsor came to me for cooperation again.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:11.000
And also asked to sign a few more contracts.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.520
This is the signal.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:15.560
This video looks bad in my eyes.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:18.520
But the sponsor is still willing to find me again, which shows that

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:21.520
The data he saw was of very high quality.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.360
This gave me a lot of confidence.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.600
Let me know where my business value is.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:27.800
Speaking of sponsors

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:31.080
I must thank the channel's long-term sponsor here.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.600
Interactive Brokers

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.800
I have been cooperating with IB for more than two years.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.240
Such a long period of cooperation

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:39.480
They gave me great creative freedom and support.

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:43.000
This is also a very valuable and real signal for me.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:43.520
For me,

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:46.320
IB is not just a partner of the channel.

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:48.960
It is also the brokerage I use for my personal investments.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.920
It is precisely because I used their services that a transaction occurred.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.280
and thus generated trust.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.560
Then I was willing to cooperate with them.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:57.200
to recommend their products.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:00.320
This is a way to build trust through transactions.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.960
Then a virtuous cycle of supply.

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:03.800
So if you are interested in investing

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:06.120
I strongly recommend everyone to use IB.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.360
You can check the link in our description.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.440
Your clicks will benefit me.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.960
This is also a form of support for me.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.400
Okay, now let's talk about trading.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.400
I know a lot of people are afraid to trade.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.920
This may be precisely because we know

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:21.560
Trading will give us the most direct and real signal.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.880
So we dare not face this truth.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:25.920
Because we are afraid of failure.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:27.800
But whether you dare or not

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.160
The truth is there.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.280
The sooner you know the truth, the more important it is to you.

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:34.720
Because when you don't have this signal

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.200
You are actually living in a state of self-paralysis.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:41.000
even in a more painful and confused state.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.200
It's like when I wasn't seriously doing business monetization.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:47.360
I had doubts about myself for a long time.

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:48.800
I don't know what I'm doing.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:50.320
Can I keep going?

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.400
But when the Yikou XinFan community went online

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.480
Someone came in at the 30th second.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:55.840
After two years

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:59.440
There are still many original partners who are still active.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:00.760
I know, OK.

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:04.040
My stuff has value in the hearts of the audience.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.840
He is willing to vote for me.

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:07.080
This gave me confidence.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.400
Let me be my true self.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:09.720
Say what I want to say.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:11.120
Including even making this video.

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:13.440
It's also me and a friend from the community.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.640
We talked about it during our coffee chat.

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:18.920
I said this video of mine might be a bit controversial again.

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:20.440
He said it's okay, Ray.

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:22.520
It's okay for you to be yourself.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:24.560
This is what we really want to see.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:27.840
And so you have the video you're watching now.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:28.440
OK

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:31.040
We use the 1% rule to question noise.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:33.400
Get real signals through trading.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:36.400
But even the most realistic transaction data

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.760
may also fluctuate in the short term.

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:39.760
bring misleading.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:42.400
So my third mental model is

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:46.360
Signals come more from long-term trends.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:48.840
rather than short-term fluctuations.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.400
We often say in investing

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:53.920
You should focus on long-term trends.

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.200
I've shared this before.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:58.280
An author I really like, Taleb, said in his book

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:00.440
Mathematically, you can actually prove that

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:02.760
In investing, when you set the observation range

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.120
When it becomes extremely short

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:05.840
The signal-to-noise ratio is reduced.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.760
The proportion of noise will become much larger.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:08.760
Besides investment

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:10.280
In entrepreneurship and life

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:12.240
This rule also holds true.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.400
Let's take my new community as an example.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:17.040
The number of people who came in the first three days of launch was very exaggerated.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.040
All the teachers were very excited.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:21.280
But then the speed slowed down.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.120
After a price increase

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.920
The speed of joining has dropped significantly.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:27.400
The teachers began to worry.

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:28.520
But I told everyone

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.880
You don't have to worry.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:31.400
Because the data from the first three days

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:32.640
and the decline after the price adjustment.

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.240
are short-term fluctuations.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:35.840
It can be said to be noise.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.760
We may need to wait until three months

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:38.840
Even after half a year

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.840
to see a real pattern.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:43.520
This is because every time we start a new business

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:44.360
Because of the novelty

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:47.320
We are easily attracted by temporary data.

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:48.840
Today's sales are very high.

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:50.760
It's easy to create a linear misunderstanding.

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.640
Assuming it will be like this every day in the future.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:53.840
Then one day the data drops.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:56.600
It feels like the end of the world is coming.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:59.800
This is because you are focusing on a specific point in time.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.720
What you observe is more noise.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:05.400
What you really need to do is to look at it over a long period of time.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:07.360
Observe a long-term trend.

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:08.520
Long enough time

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.800
Only then can you observe the pattern.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:11.840
The reason why I'm not panicking is

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.160
It's because I've experienced so much of this.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.960
Experience from zero to one.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.040
My experience is

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.040
Don't be nervous.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.680
Don't panic because of temporary gains and losses.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.920
We should trust the process.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.160
Let the bullets fly for a while.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:27.480
Actually, life is like this too.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:29.080
There are many important signals in life.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.680
all need to be obtained through long-term investment.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:35.680
And we have two perspectives to lengthen the dimension.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:37.320
One is to look back at the past.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.440
Look at yourself last year or even five years ago.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:40.640
and yourself now.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.400
What is the overall trend?

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:43.960
Are you always changing?

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:44.960
always getting better.

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:45.640
If so,

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:48.320
That means you are on the right track.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:50.560
The other is to look forward.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:52.560
Be a time traveler.

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:55.200
Imagine yourself a year from now, five years from now.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.840
The decisions you make now

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.440
What kind of impact will you have at that time?

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:01.240
Through this kind of time travel

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:02.720
Put yourself in the future.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.680
Look back at today from a reverse perspective.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.120
can provide you with very important signals.

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.240
OK, the first three models are more about

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:12.560
About how to interpret signals from the outside world.

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.560
But eventually these signals

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:17.640
needs to be filtered and judged by yourself.

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:22.200
This requires the introduction of an inward-looking signal filtering model.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:24.640
A couple of days ago, I received a book I shared before.

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:27.240
A letter from Paul, the author of Pathless Path.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.720
He said his traditional Chinese version is already on the market in Taiwan.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:31.800
The simplified Chinese version will also be published soon.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:33.720
He wants to send me a few of his signed books.

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:36.320
Because he found that many Chinese readers told him

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:37.680
are all through my videos.

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:38.800
I know about his book.

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.800
This is a little thank you from him.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:41.960
But what I want to say is

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:43.720
I'm the one who really needs to be thanked.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.480
Because through conversation with him

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:46.600
I have benefited a lot.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:48.360
I learned a very important point.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.280
That is your energy.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.360
is a crucial signal filter in life.

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:55.520
For example, if you are facing a new opportunity,

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:57.080
I feel that it is giving you more energy.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.360
Just like he said in the book

00:13:58.360 --> 00:13:59.440
If you feel that

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:00.280
Hell yeah

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:02.360
Then this is a correct signal.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.680
If you find yourself facing something

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:06.360
It's draining your energy.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.480
Your whole body is resisting.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:10.760
Then this is a signal to tell you

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:13.240
Maybe you shouldn't do this.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.880
It's been over a year since I visited Paul.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:15.600
In this year

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.600
Especially after I went through a health crisis

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:20.280
Using energy as a signal

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:22.920
has become a principle I practice every day.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:23.960
And in this year

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.840
I have a new understanding of it.

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.760
If using energy as a signal is

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.720
Listen to your body

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.200
Then the fifth model

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:32.840
Following your intuition is

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:34.080
Listen to your heart

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:35.160
It can even be said that

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:36.680
Listen to the universe

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.520
We read a book in our community called

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.280
Don't believe everything you think

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:41.720
Its core point is

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:43.480
Don't overthink it.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.920
You have to follow your intuition.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:46.920
What does that mean?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:50.200
Many of our important ideas and intuitions

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:52.120
are because of overthinking

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.840
let it disappear without becoming a reality.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:56.080
It says in this book

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:58.880
Overthinking is not normal thinking.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:02.840
It is more brought about by our human instinct of fear.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:04.280
In our long-term evolution

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:06.280
have an instinctual fear of failure.

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:08.680
Because in the long primitive period

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:11.280
The consequence of failure is often death.

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:12.800
So we will over-judge

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.520
Try every means to avoid failure.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:17.760
So this leads to when we have an intuition

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:19.640
We will think of all kinds of possibilities of failure.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.000
The obstacles we may encounter

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.880
The preparations that may need to be made

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:24.880
This often leads to many of our ideas

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:26.080
not put into practice.

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:29.840
Because staying put is the safest thing to do.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:31.480
But we often overlook that in modern society

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:35.000
The consequences of failure for many ideas and opportunities are very low.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.120
But the potential upside is very high.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:40.880
So although overthinking stems from our survival instinct

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:42.280
But in modern society

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:45.160
It often suppresses our true intuition.

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:46.680
generate internal noise.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:48.560
And the one that initially made you feel energetic

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:50.120
The intuition that excites you

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:52.320
may be the real signal.

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:55.080
This reminds me of the book The Creative Act.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:58.280
It mentions that your thoughts are actually given to you by the universe.

00:15:58.280 --> 00:15:59.760
When you have an idea

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:01.120
As a creator

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:03.720
You are obliged to pass it on.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:05.960
Yes, what you are doing is not creating.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.360
but to deliver.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:10.400
Turn this idea from the universe into reality.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.360
If you overthink it

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.000
Hesitated and didn't do this.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.200
And someone else did it.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:18.160
You might think someone stole your idea.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:22.080
But in fact, you have not fulfilled your responsibility as a creator.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.800
Bring this idea to the world.

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:25.800
So it found another carrier.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:27.480
came to this world.

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:29.160
Looking back at my AI community

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:32.920
It's probably the fastest startup project in my life.

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:36.120
From idea to execution, it only took two weeks.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:37.680
I was thinking at the time

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:39.440
With such a community

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:41.400
It's definitely helpful to people.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:43.560
And this is exactly where my passion lies.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:46.120
So I did what I said I would do.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.600
If I had thought about it then

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:49.720
What if people judge me and I fail?

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:51.120
What if no one signs up?

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:53.520
Maybe I haven't even started yet.

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:57.280
Then I might not have gotten the precious signals I have now.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:16:59.240
drowned in noise.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:01.320
True failure is not failure after trying.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:03.720
but you didn't even try.

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:05.440
Trapped by overthinking

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:08.200
When someone else does what you want to do but don't dare to do

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:09.200
You feel offended.

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:10.520
I feel that others are not worthy.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:11.800
But this is your problem.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:15.040
Because you didn't listen to your intuition and energy.

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:17.080
These two very valuable signals.

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:20.280
You have not fulfilled your responsibility as a creator.

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:24.520
Pass on the signal from the universe and make it a reality.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:26.080
Finally, I want to share

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.720
The book we read in September

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:30.400
A quote from The Lean Learning

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:33.280
The richest place in the world is the cemetery.

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:38.320
Because there are countless novel ideas buried there that were never realized.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.520
These buried ideas, in my opinion,

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:43.200
It's not just a lack of courage.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.520
More likely,

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:49.160
They don't know what the real signals and noises of life are.

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.320
They are disturbed by external comments.

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:53.440
Confused by short-term fluctuations

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:57.400
and hindered by their own inner fear and overthinking.

00:17:57.400 --> 00:18:01.200
In the end, I failed to follow my true energy and intuition to act.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:02.800
to get the signals of life.

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:05.160
Walk your own path.

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:08.280
I hope the five models shared today can help you.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:09.240
Thanks for watching.

